{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310646,"nonce":"6c6dlSJrgoOV0Q9U9kJv1e3MtMA=","title":"Conformance is 367 on BOTH mac and real Linux; CI's lower number is runner artifacts, not platform divergence","message":"Measured 2026-08-28 at 19cf2ab0, mac arm64 vs the NUC (ubuntu x86-64, 16 core),\nboth with CI's exact env (TIMEOUT=25, JOBS=4, RAYZOR_PROFILE_LOAD=1,\nRAYZOR_TIER_TRACE_STARTUP=1):\n\n    PASS 367 on both.  COMPILE_FAIL 259 on both.\n\nOnly 10 of 1165 tests differ, and the two that touch the score CANCEL:\nIssue4649 passes on mac only, Issue11535 on Linux only. The other 8 are\nalready-failing tests that fail *differently* (WRONG_ANSWER vs CRASH).\n\n**CI's 363 is not a Linux number.** The ubuntu runner is 4 vCPU (2 cores + SMT):\n  - 32 tests it scores TIMEOUT all CRASH on the NUC — same defect, and the\n    25s limit covers compile+run, so a slow runner reclassifies them.\n  - TIMEOUT swings 30/42/34/35 across four consecutive CI runs, and PASS moves\n    inversely. 20 tests time out in ALL four; 11-15 flap. Treat any CI\n    conformance delta under ~5 as noise.\n  - 3 tests (Issue12089, Issue5569, Issue8717) score NO_OUTPUT on CI but PASS on\n    BOTH real machines. UNEXPLAINED: the retained CI log contains\n    `CONFORMANCE_OK` as line 1 and run.sh's PASS test is `grep -q\n    '^CONFORMANCE_OK'` on that same captured string. No duplicate rows. Do not\n    invent a cause for this without reproducing it.\n\nTRAP that cost a whole first run: the NUC's corpus checkout was STALE — sparse\nlist `tests/unit/src/unit` instead of `tests/unit/src`, so `misc/` and\n`scripthost/` were missing and Issue9394/Issue5351 failed as fake platform bugs.\n`./haxe-conformance/fetch.sh` repairs it. **Run fetch.sh on any box before\nquoting its score.**\n\nThreads are NOT a driver of platform failures: 1 of 194 CI crashes uses threads.\nClosures appear in 40 of 194, but the one closure test that diverged\n(Issue5569, closures of differing arity in a Map) passes on real Linux.\n\nReal Linux-only suite failure: `test_single_f32` — see\n[[bugs_single_plus_f64_literal_broken_three_of_four]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_mac_and_linux_conformance_are_identical` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}